{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "7b2c3918-2a64-489a-8350-888a6323296d",
    "name": "School Attendance Management API - Complete",
    "description": "Complete Postman collection generated from the Spring Boot backend controllers in server-attendance-implementation.zip.\n\nIncludes every HTTP controller operation: authentication (3), admin (7), rooms/classrooms (8), students (3), RFID (7), timetable (3), attendance (8), total 39 requests.\n\nQUICK START\n1. Import this collection and the companion environment JSON.\n2. Select the environment and set baseUrl if your server is not http://localhost:4200.\n3. Set loginUsername/loginPassword. The supplied application.properties defaults are admin/admin only when those environment overrides are not set.\n4. Run 00 - Authentication / Login. The JWT response.token is saved to authToken automatically.\n5. Use admin credentials for admin setup endpoints. Then log in as a teacher to test teacher-scoped routes; each login replaces authToken.\n6. Create a room, create a classroom, manually set classroomId if not available from the current API response, create students, assign students, configure timetable, enroll RFID, assign the chip and test attendance.\n\nIMPORTANT BACKEND-SPECIFIC NOTES\n- This collection contains all HTTP REST controller mappings, not MQTT topics. The ESP32's RFID scan path uses Mosquitto, not an HTTP endpoint.\n- POST /api/attendance/checkin/{studentId} is an ADMIN-only manual check-in endpoint. Normal RFID check-ins are received through MQTT.\n- MQTT topics (from MqttService): server publishes attendance/server/setRfid (JSON {requestId}); server subscribes attendance/reader/set (JSON {requestId,uid} or legacy plain UID) and attendance/reader/scan (plain UID). Server publishes attendance/server/setResult, attendance/server/scanResult and attendance/server/status.\n- RFID status polling requires the ESP32 to publish the result to attendance/reader/set after the admin starts enrollment.\n- Timetable writes require startTime and checkoutTime in HH:mm:ss format. Day path variable is an uppercase Java DayOfWeek name.\n- School-local date defaults to Europe/Berlin. Collection pre-request script provides {{today}} for read/attendance-day requests.\n- POST /api/auth/admin/createUser expects displayname (lowercase field name), username, password and optional role. Supported roles are ADMIN and TEACHER; omitting role defaults to TEACHER.\n- POST /api/classroom currently returns only \"Classroom Created!\", not the created ID. Set environment variable classroomId manually after creating the classroom. GET /api/classroom/my can populate it for a user whose myClassroom was set with assignMyClassroom.\n- POST /api/attendance/student/{id} is a legacy duplicate of the GET read operation; GET is preferred.\n- Logout returns LoggedOut=true but does not revoke a stateless JWT on the server; clear authToken manually or run a new login.\n- Optional date query parameters on the checkout/session requests are disabled by default; the backend defaults to the school-local current date.\n\nExpected status codes and role requirements are described on each request.\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "39409072"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "00 - Authentication",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (saves JWT automatically)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Login returns 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "let data = {};",
                  "try { data = pm.response.json(); } catch (e) { /* Empty body on failed login is valid API behavior. */ }",
                  "if (data && data.token) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set(\"authToken\", data.token);",
                  "  pm.test(\"JWT token saved to authToken\", function () { pm.expect(data.token).to.be.a(\"string\").and.not.empty; });",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.test(\"Response contains token\", function () { pm.expect(data && data.token, \"Expected { token: ... }\").to.exist; });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{loginUsername}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{loginPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public endpoint. Uses loginUsername/loginPassword environment variables. On HTTP 200, the test script saves response.token into authToken for all subsequent requests. Default credentials in the supplied application.properties are admin/admin unless overridden by deployment environment variables."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "logout"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Authenticated endpoint. This API currently returns LoggedOut=true; JWTs are stateless and are not revoked server-side. Clear authToken in the environment when finished."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Change password on first login",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"oldPassword\": \"{{oldPassword}}\",\n  \"newPassword\": \"{{newPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/changePasswordOnFirstLogin",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "users",
                "changePasswordOnFirstLogin"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Authenticated. Changes the password for the currently authenticated user. New password must be at least 10 characters. The old password must match."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
